### Notes about planning the computation ###

- First we want to sort the input. 
    How many classes per <g,q>? 
    Some part of the computation might be done only on a subset of the input.
    I would put the `biggest' <g,q> at the end, so that we can interrupt the computation.
- How many scripts?
    I'd say 3:
    a) schema WKClasses
    b) pAdicPosElt (only ordinary; expensive comp of GaloisGroup)
    c) polarizations of degrees [1,4,9,25] (depends on the expensive comp of Pic).
    
    a) and b) are independent from each other.
    a) should be very fast.
    c) depends on both a) and b).
